 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Admissible blow-up",
 "statement": "Let $T$ be quasi-compact and quasi-separated and $U\\subseteq T$ a\nquasi-compact open. For a finite-type quasi-coherent ideal\n$\\mathcal I\\subseteq\\mathcal O_T$ with $\\mathcal I|_U=\\mathcal O_U$, the\nblow-up\n\n$$\nb:\\operatorname{Bl}_{\\mathcal I}(T)=\n\\operatorname{Proj}_T\\Bigl(\\bigoplus_{m\\geq0}\\mathcal I^m\\Bigr)\n\\longrightarrow T\n$$\n\nis called *$U$-admissible*. Its center is disjoint from $U$.",
 "source": {
